==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|keusanan|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|geus-|taste, choose|lang=ang}}.  Cognate with Old Frisian ''kiāsa'', Old Saxon [[kiosan]] (Dutch [[kiezen]]), Old High German [[kiosan]], Old Norse ''kjósa'', Gothic [[𐌺𐌹𐌿𐍃𐌰𐌽]].  The Indo-European root was also the source of Latin [[gustare]] ‘to taste’, Albanian [[desha]] ‘chosen’.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈʧeːozɑn/|lang=ang}}

